 "adjudicate": [
  {
   "id": "0180_R5_baptism_02",
   "text": "сятъ второго года Октя-",
   "status": "image_checked",
   "note": "After 'второр' the letter is a round о, so второго (not втораго). Октя is О-к-т-я, with т as three minims under a faint bar. A short tick follows я before the hyphen; I read it as part of the hyphen stroke. The curved stroke at the far right edge is a flourish and is not transcribed."
  },
  {
   "id": "0180_R5_baptism_03",
   "text": "бря [пятнадцатаго?]",
   "status": "draft",
   "note": "Ending -надцатаго is clear. The start reads п (n-form), then я with a leg, then т (m-form with an overbar flourish), so пятнадцатаго. That matches parents_08 (born Oct 15, baptised the same day). одиннадцатаго (A) would put baptism before birth. I see no separate 'и' after бря (B)."
  },
  {
   "id": "0180_R5_baptism_04",
   "text": "дня въ [Плунгянскомъ?]",
   "status": "draft",
   "note": "End of the town adjective is crowded: after -ско there is an extra glyph before a clear 'мъ', maybe a correction. The formula word is likely, but the letters do not align cleanly."
  },
  {
   "id": "0180_R5_baptism_06",
   "text": "стелѣ Мѣстнымъ",
   "status": "image_checked",
